\section{Relinking the Residual Context After Partial Handling}

A handler can discharge only some of the requirements of a suspended
computation. Consider a toy typed linker for boxes whose assumptions
are keyed by binder identity. Input is a checked box, a table of
local implementations for part of its context, and a map from each
remaining assumption to an operation in the enclosing context.
Assume exact signature matching and that the local implementations
cannot perform any operations of their own. The output is a new
box over the residual operation context or a linking diagnostic.
This linking step changes the interpretation of operations without
running the suspended body; explicit resumption handling remains
part of the runtime model.

\begin{sudocode}
  \Input box $(\Psi,c)$, interpretations $H$, forwarding map $F$
  \Output relinked box or diagnostic
  \State $L\gets$ empty binding map; $\Phi\gets$ empty context
  \ForAll{assumption $(i,T)$ in $\Psi$}
    \If{$i$ is in $H$}
      \State $L[i]\gets\Call{CheckHandler}{H[i],T}$ or fail
      \Comment{No residual effects from this clause}
    \Else
      \State $j\gets\Call{CheckTarget}{F[i],T}$ or fail
      \State $L[i]\gets\Call{Forward}{j}$
      \State insert $(j,T)$ in $\Phi$ \Comment{Dedup by identity}
    \EndIf
  \EndFor
  \State \Return $\Call{RelinkBox}{\Phi,c,L}$
\end{sudocode}

Take a box that obtains $x$ from $\mathsf{read}()$, sends $x+1$
to $\mathsf{emit}$, then returns $2x$. The signatures are
$\mathsf{Unit}\to\mathsf{Int}$ and
$\mathsf{Int}\to\mathsf{Unit}$, respectively. Supply a
read handler that resumes with $6$, and map the old emit
identity $12$ to a compatible audit operation with identity
$43$. The new box requires only audit. Running it in an
environment that logs audit requests records $7$ and returns
$12$. Running the linking procedure alone records nothing.
If audit instead expects a string, linking fails before any
of these computations take place.

Every original operation reference must still resolve to exactly
one interpretation with its original argument and resume types.
Relinking affects only the free operation references described by
$\Psi$; a nested box with its own operation named \texttt{emit}
is not rewritten by spelling. If local clauses can perform their
own operations, the residual context must include their
dependencies too. Deduplicating two forward links is valid only
when the caller has explicitly chosen the same target identity
for both; the linker must not infer that choice from equal
signatures.
